; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Squiral
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     squares, spirals, REPEAT, color, variables
; SUMMARY:  Squares that grow a little and turn a little each time stack up into a whirling "squiral".
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Draws 60 squares around the same corner. Each one is a bit bigger
;   than the last and turned a few degrees, and each has its own color.
;   On the right, a second squiral uses outlines only, so you can see
;   the separate squares that make up the whirl.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then change the numbers in the two calls at the bottom:
;   the number of squares, how much each one grows, and how far it turns.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a SQUARE procedure with a size input
;   * a variable that changes inside REPEAT
;   * how small changes, repeated, add up to a curve
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Turn by 15 instead of 9, or by -9 to whirl the other way.
;   * Grow by 1.1 instead of 1.05 (the squares get big fast).
;   * Use triangles instead of squares.
; ============================================================

; Square spirals, often nicknamed "squirals", have been drawn in Logo
; classrooms since the turtle first appeared. They show how a gentle
; change, repeated many times, makes a curve out of straight lines.

to square :size
  repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]
end

; A filled square, colored by its number N. Three sine waves, a third
; of a circle apart, walk the color smoothly around the rainbow.
to colored.square :size :n
  setpencolor [30 30 45]
  filled (list 150 + 100 * sin :n * 6  150 + 100 * sin :n * 6 + 120  150 + 100 * sin :n * 6 + 240) [square :size]
end

; Each FILLED square covers the ones drawn before it. If we started
; small, the big squares would hide everything. So we draw backwards:
; the biggest square first, the smallest last. Square number N has size
; 8 times GROW to the power N - 1, and is turned (N - 1) times TURN.
to squiral :count :grow :turn
  localmake "h heading
  for [n :count 1] [
    setheading :h + (:n - 1) * :turn
    colored.square 8 * power :grow :n - 1 :n
  ]
end

to line.squiral :count :grow :turn
  localmake "size 6
  repeat :count [
    setpencolor (list 60 + repcount * 2.5 220 - repcount * 2 255)
    square :size
    right :turn
    make "size :size * :grow
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [30 30 45]
setpensize 1
penup setxy -160 50 setheading 0 pendown
squiral 60 1.05 9
penup setxy 250 -30 setheading 0 pendown
setpensize 2
line.squiral 72 1.04 10
